# basedpyright Safety

RULE: Never run `basedpyright .` or `basedpyright` without source dir. Always use `timeout 120 basedpyright <source_dir>/`. For audits, run quality gates per repo, NOT standalone basedpyright.
WHY: 30+ repo workspace — `basedpyright .` consumes 4-16GB RAM and spawns zombie processes.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md

DO:
  timeout 120 basedpyright unified_trading_services/
  run_timeout 120 basedpyright <source_dir>/   # use run_timeout helper — see codex QG template SSOT
  cd repo && bash scripts/quality-gates.sh --no-fix  # for audits

NEVER:
  basedpyright .  # analyzes entire workspace
  basedpyright  # no args
  cd repo && basedpyright .  # still wrong
